# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Docker compose data dir
.docker

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# user-customized env file
.env

# compiled program
ranger-ims-go
compose.ranger-ims-go

node_modules

# the default dir for storing attachments
ims-attachments

# the temp dir for `go tool air`
air_tmp

# Generated code — NOT committed. All of it is produced at build time by
# `go run bin/build/build.go` (use `-generate-only` to skip the final compile),
# and also in the Docker build + CI. One convention: no generated code in the tree.
#   buf   -> /gen/
#   sqlc  -> store/imsdb/, directory/clubhousedb/
#   templ -> web/template/*_templ.go
#   tsgo  -> web/static/*.js
/gen/
/store/imsdb/
/directory/clubhousedb/
/web/template/*_templ.go
/web/static/*.js
